# PENDING - fails today. RFC 9293 3.10.7.3, SYN-SENT: a RST is acceptable only
# if its ACK acknowledges our SYN; "if the RST bit is set ... if the ACK bit is
# off, drop the segment and return". A blind RST without ACK must not abort
# the open, so the real SYN-ACK that follows still completes it.
0      connect 9000
+0     > S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 0,wscale 1>
+0.005 < R 0:0(0) win 0
+0     state SYN_SENT
+0.005 < S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460>
+0     > . 1:1(0) ack 1
+0     state ESTABLISHED
